Yes, you can remove the blank line after \end{knitrout}, but even you<br>do that, the following text is still a separate paragraph in default<br>knitr LaTeX output. Here is how to do it (set the &#39;document&#39; hook to<br>replace &#39;\end{knitrout}
&#39;):<br><br>\documentclass{article}<br><br> egin{document}<br><br>Knitr replaces 	exttt{@} with an empty string so that it becomes a<br>blank line in the tex output.<br><br>&lt;&lt;setup&gt;&gt;=<br>knit_hooks$set(document = function(x) {<br>  gsub(&#39;(\\end\{knitrout\})
&#39;, &#39;\1&#39;, x)<br>})<br>@<br><br>See if it works.<br>&lt;&lt;&gt;&gt;=<br># hello world<br>1+1<br>@<br>This line should continue as a part of the above paragraph instead of<br>a separate paragraph.<br><br>\end{document}<br><br><br>This is due to the kframe environment (anything after it becomes a new<br>paragraph). If you want the Sweave style, you can simply use<br>render_sweave() (it will set all the options you mentioned). But at<br>the moment, there is a tiny problem that I need to solve (will do it<br>soon).<br><br>That said, an alternative way to solve this problem is to add<br>
oindent automatically, e.g.<br><br>knit_hooks$set(document = function(x) {<br>  gsub(&#39;(\\end\{knitrout\}[
]+)&#39;, &#39;\1\\noindent &#39;, x)<br>})<br><br>Regards,<br>Yihui<br>--<br>Yihui Xie &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">xiey...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>Phone: <a href="tel:(515)%20294-2465" value="+15152942465" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">515-294-2465</a> Web: <a href="http://yihui.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://yihui.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792355391041000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kFZjcwee8fdlbmhPF21OS">http://yihui.name</a><br>Department of Statistics, Iowa State University<br>2215 Snedecor Hall, Ames, IA<br><br><br>On Wed, Aug 8, 2012 at 11:49 AM, Douglas Bates &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">dmb...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt; My global opts_chunk contains tidy=FALSE, prompt=TRUE, comment=&#39;&#39; because I<br>&gt; would like to reproduce Sweave-style chunks.  I find that there is a blank<br>&gt; line following the knitrout environment in the .tex file I produce so that<br>&gt;<br>&gt; &lt;&lt;lm1&gt;&gt;=<br>&gt; lm1 &lt;- lm(log(conc) ~ sqrt(age), PCB)<br>&gt; @<br>&gt; Model-fitting functions in \proglang{R} produce an object of a<br>&gt;<br>&gt; becomes<br>&gt;<br>&gt;  egin{knitrout}<br>&gt; \definecolor{shadecolor}{rgb}{0.969, 0.969,<br>&gt; 0.969}\color{fgcolor} egin{kframe}<br>&gt;  egin{alltt}<br>&gt;&gt; lm1 &lt;- \hlfunctioncall{lm}(\hlfunctioncall{log}(conc) ~<br>&gt;&gt; \hlfunctioncall{sqrt}(age), PCB)<br>&gt; \end{alltt}<br>&gt; \end{kframe}<br>&gt; \end{knitrout}<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Model-fitting functions in \proglang{R} produce an object of a<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Is there a way to suppress that blank line?  I would prefer not to need to<br>&gt; add 
